  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 300 AM Saturday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... A continuation of dry and seasonable conditions is \nexpected through next week. \n\nAn initially high amplitude mid and upr-level ridge over the MS \nValley will dampen while progressing slowly ewd and across the \nSoutheast through next week, where it may remain through next \nweekend. To the east of the slowly progressive and dampening ridge, \na moisture-starved shortwave trough will dig across the Middle \nAtlantic and offshore through this weekend. \n\nAt the surface, a series of reinforcing, Canadian surface highs will \nprogress across the Great Lakes and Middle Atlantic and extend \nacross cntl NC through next week (and probably through next \nweekend), while modifying/moderating. A prolonged period of dry and \nseasonable conditions will result, with a gradual moderation of \ntemperatures likely late next week through Halloween weekend.",
